"opening": "The marshmallow library is introducing new field types for IP interfaces and refining error handling for method fields. The marshmallow-jsonschema consumer must align with these changes to ensure correct schema generation and robust error reporting.",
"requirements": [
{
"id": "m08",
"text": "In the marshmallow library, the public names IPInterface, IPv4Interface, IPv6, and IPv6Interface must be available as distinct field classes within the fields module. These fields must correctly serialize and deserialize IP interface objects according to standard networking formats."
},
{
"id": "m16",
"text": "In the marshmallow library, when a Schema class references a method name in a Method field that does not exist on the schema instance, it must raise an AttributeError during schema initialization rather than at runtime. The public name set_value remains accessible for use in custom validation logic within these methods."
}
]
